      "writtenOn": "2019-07-16T17:17:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This makes foreign projects not include it. We have to check all foreign projects can still compile. In my search, I found attestation, biod, g2f_tools, and trunks depend on chromeos-ec-headers, which installs compile_time_macros.h under /usr/include/chromeos/ec/.\n\nThe only macro ec_commands.h needs compile_time_macros.h for is BIT(), which is now defined here for foreign projects. So, I think this change is still good (even it breaks a foreign project).\n\nIf a foreign project breaks because of this change, it\u0027s broken legitimately. We should make such a project include a proper header file. For example, if biod uses ARRAY_SIZE, it should be defined locally not by EC\u0027s compile_time_macros.h.\n\nChromium EC should export only its commands not generic compile time macros.",
